.TH TNT-MODULE-PROTOCOL 7 "2026-09-08" "TNT 1.3.1"
.SH NAME
tnt-module-protocol \- implement an external TNT message module
.SH DESCRIPTION
TNT modules are external processes that exchange UTF-8 JSON Lines records
with the server through standard input and standard output.
The supported protocol identifier is
.BR tnt.module.v1 .
.P
Modules receive selected public message events and may create public
plain-text messages.
The core chat path continues when an individual module is invalid, slow,
stopped, or saturated.
.SH ACTIVATION
Modules are disabled unless
.B TNT_MODULE_PATHS
contains a colon-separated list of module directories.
The combined value must contain at most 4095 bytes.
TNT enables at most eight successfully loaded modules.
An oversized combined value makes server initialization fail.
.P
For each directory, TNT reads
.I tnt-module.json
and starts its declared entrypoint with the module directory as the working
directory.
No command-line arguments are supplied.
.SH MANIFEST
The manifest is a JSON object of at most 4094 bytes.
The following fields are required:
.TP
.B protocol
String equal to
.BR tnt.module.v1 .
.TP
.B name
Stable module identifier of at most 56 ASCII characters.
It may contain lowercase letters, digits, and hyphens.
It must start and end
with a letter or digit.
.TP
.B entrypoint
Nonempty executable path relative to the module directory.
It must not start with
.BR / ,
contain
.BR .. ,
contain whitespace or control bytes, or contain any of
.BR "| ; & ` $ < > \e" .
.TP
.B permissions
Array containing both
.B message:read
and
.BR message:create .
.TP
.B events
Array containing
.BR message.created .
.P
Unknown manifest fields are ignored by the runtime.
The
.B version
field is an unprefixed MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH release identifier used by the
companion module repository's validation tools.
The runtime does not inspect it.
Similarly,
.B tnt_min_version
is advisory to deployment tools rather than a runtime compatibility check.
.P
A minimal manifest is:
.P
.EX
{
  "protocol": "tnt.module.v1",
  "name": "echo",
  "entrypoint": "./echo-module",
  "permissions": ["message:read", "message:create"],
  "events": ["message.created"]
}
.EE
.SH TRANSPORT
TNT writes protocol records to the module's standard input.
The module writes response records to standard output and may write
diagnostics to standard error.
.P
Each input or output record is one complete JSON object followed by one
newline.
The JSON payload before the newline may contain at most 4094 bytes.
Standard output must contain no banners, logging, blank lines, or other
text.
.P
Unknown members of a recognized object must be ignored.
String values use JSON escaping and decode to valid UTF-8.
.SH HANDSHAKE
Immediately after starting a module,
TNT sends one handshake record containing
these values:
.TP
.B type
String
.BR handshake .
.TP
.B protocol
String
.BR tnt.module.v1 .
.TP
.B server.name
String
.BR tnt .
.TP
.B server.version
The running TNT version string.
.P
For TNT 1.3.1, the record is:
.P
.EX
{"type":"handshake","protocol":"tnt.module.v1",\c
"server":{"name":"tnt","version":"1.3.1"}}
.EE
.P
The module must answer within two seconds with:
.P
.EX
{"type":"handshake.ok","protocol":"tnt.module.v1"}
.EE
.P
Additional members in
.B handshake.ok
are ignored.
Any other response, timeout, or I/O failure prevents that module from being
enabled.
.SH EVENTS
For each eligible public message, TNT sends an object with
.B type
set to
.B message.created
and a
.B message
object containing:
.TP
.B id
An opaque string of the form
.BR local-N .
.TP
.B timestamp
UTC timestamp in the form
.BR YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ .
.TP
.B sender
The public message sender string.
.TP
.B kind
String
.BR text .
.TP
.B plain_text
The public plain-text content.
.TP
.B metadata
An object, currently empty.
.P
For example, the following is one JSON Lines record:
.P
.EX
{"type":"message.created","message":{\c
"id":"local-1","timestamp":"2026-06-04T12:00:00Z",\c
"sender":"alice","kind":"text","plain_text":"hello",\c
"metadata":{}}}
.EE
.P
Interactive public messages and exec
.B post
messages generate events.
Private messages, room lifecycle notices, and module-created messages
produce no events.
Module-created messages are not fed back into the module set.
.SH RESPONSES
For each
.B message.created
event, a module may write zero or more
.B message.create
records and must finish with one
.B event.ok
record.
.P
Create a public message with:
.P
.EX
{"type":"message.create","plain_text":"echo: hello"}
.EE
.P
.B plain_text
must contain 1 through 1023 UTF-8 bytes.
A line feed is the only C0 or C1 control character it may contain; every
other one, and DEL, is refused.
The log stores a line feed escaped, so it costs two of the 1023 bytes.
TNT persists and broadcasts accepted text with sender
.BI module: name .
.P
Finish the event with:
.P
.EX
{"type":"event.ok"}
.EE
.P
At most eight response records are accepted for one event, including the
final acknowledgement.
A module can therefore create at most seven messages for one event.
All responses for the event must arrive within one deadline, 100
milliseconds by default and set by
.BR TNT_MODULE_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_MS .
No record may follow
.B event.ok
for that event.
.P
An unrecognized response type, invalid JSON, invalid text, blank line, or
output after the response limit is a protocol failure.
The protocol has no accepted
.B error
response type.
.SH FAILURE HANDLING
A handshake failure skips the affected module.
After activation, a write failure, write timeout, read failure, response
timeout, or response-count overflow disables the module process.
.P
Three invalid responses without an intervening valid response disable a
module.
Messages created before a later failure in the same event remain persisted
and visible.
.P
Each module has a queue of 128 pending events.
When it is full, TNT drops new events for that module and continues serving
chat traffic.
.P
On server shutdown, TNT sends SIGTERM to each module process group.
After 500 milliseconds, remaining processes are sent SIGKILL.
.SH LIMITS
.TP
.B 8
Maximum enabled modules.
.TP
.B 4094 bytes
Maximum manifest size and maximum JSON Lines payload size.
.TP
.B 2 seconds
Handshake read and write deadline.
.TP
.B 250 milliseconds
Per-event write deadline from TNT to a module.
.TP
.B 100 milliseconds
Default whole response deadline for one event.
.BR TNT_MODULE_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_MS
sets it, from 10 to 5000.
.TP
.B 8 records
Maximum responses per event, including
.BR event.ok .
.TP
.B 128 events
Pending queue capacity per module.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
The protocol identifier, required manifest capabilities, event and response
types, and documented member meanings form the
.B tnt.module.v1
contract.
.P
Future compatible senders may add members to existing objects.
Modules must ignore unknown members while continuing to validate required
members and their types.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I module-directory/tnt-module.json
Module manifest.
.TP
.I module-directory/entrypoint
Executable selected by the manifest.
.SH CAVEATS
A module is not an operating-system sandbox.
It runs as the TNT service account.
It can access every resource available to that account.
Use a dedicated account and operating-system isolation for untrusted
modules.
.P
The child inherits most of the server environment.
TNT removes
.BR TNT_ACCESS_TOKEN ,
.BR LD_PRELOAD ,
and
.BR LD_LIBRARY_PATH .
On macOS it also removes
.B DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES
and
.BR DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH .
Other deployment secrets can remain visible.
Do not put unrelated secrets in the server environment.
.P
Use standard error for module diagnostics.
Any diagnostic written to standard output corrupts protocol framing and may
disable the module.
.SH EXAMPLES
A module producing no message replies with exactly one line:
.P
.EX
{"type":"event.ok"}
.EE
.P
A module creating two messages replies with three lines:
.P
.EX
{"type":"message.create","plain_text":"first"}
{"type":"message.create","plain_text":"second"}
{"type":"event.ok"}
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tntctl (1),
.BR tnt\-message\-log (5),
.BR tnt\-exec (7),
.BR tnt (8)
